# Build and verify

## Layout

- Repo root contains `Red Dust Control Center/`, `Scripts/`, `Interactive Object/`.
- App cwd for Python is **`Red Dust Control Center/`** (imports `core`, `ui`, `settings`).
- Venv lives at `Red Dust Control Center/.venv` (created by setup scripts).

## Red Dust Control Center (Python / PySide6)

Prefer the project venv; do not install into system Python.

```powershell
# One-time / refresh deps (Windows)
.\Scripts\Setup venv win.bat

# Agent verify after substantive Python edits (no GUI)
& "Red Dust Control Center\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" -m compileall -q "Red Dust Control Center"
```

Launch only when the user asks:

```powershell
.\Scripts\Launch RDCC win.cmd
# or from app dir:
& ".\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" main.py
```

Other platforms: `Scripts/Setup venv mac.command`, `Scripts/Launch RDCC mac.command`, `Scripts/setup-raspberrypi.sh`, `Scripts/launch-raspberrypi.sh`. Requirements files: `requirements_windows.txt`, `requirements_mac.txt`, `requirements_raspberrypi.txt`.

**Do not** invent alternate run paths (different venv location, Debug wrappers, packaging) for routine checks.

## Interactive Object (firmware)

Two styles under `Interactive Object/`:

| Path | Toolchain |
|------|-----------|
| `Lilygo/lilygo_shaker/` (and similar `.ino` sketches) | Arduino IDE / ESP32 core — open the `.ino`, edit `settings.h`, Verify/Upload |
| `Test ESP_RGB/` (PlatformIO) | `pio run` from that folder when PlatformIO is available |

Agents should **not** flash boards unless asked. Prefer reading `settings.h` / `platformio.ini` and matching RDCC wire contracts (`SERIAL_BAUDRATE`, pin slots, OSC path/port) over guessing hardware.

When firmware and RDCC share a protocol change, update **both** sides and call that out in the summary.

## Export / portable bundle

Repo-only: `export.bat` or `Scripts/Export RDCC.ps1` → `export/red_dust.zip`. Do not run export unless the user asks.

## After edits

- Python: `compileall` (or a focused `python -c "import …"`) is enough unless the user wants a full app launch.
- Firmware: compile/verify only for the sketch you changed; skip if the toolchain is unavailable — say so briefly.
